1
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:02,400
(Episode 22)

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:04,570
Are you all right?

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:06,780
Where are you hurt?

4
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:09,380
Please, you have to help me.

5
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:14,820
Ae Sook...

6
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:16,990
Aren't you Ae Sook?

7
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,920
Joo Ae Sook from Yeongsu High, right?

8
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:22,390
Park Hee Jung?

9
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:25,990
Oh, you remember me. But what's wrong?

10
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,030
Why are you in so much pain?

11
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,030
The baby... The baby's coming.

12
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,870
What? My goodness. Let's get you to the hospital.

13
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,540
Watch your step.

14
00:00:41,510 --> 00:00:42,710
You're almost there.

15
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:44,610
All right, just a little more.

16
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:56,720
Hae Ra.

17
00:01:58,290 --> 00:01:59,290
My daughter.

18
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,730
Rather than having you live like me,

19
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:08,000
getting trampled on and losing out on everything,

20
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,700
I thought it would've been better if you had never been born.

21
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:19,470
To you,

22
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:21,810
I didn't just give life.

23
00:02:24,050 --> 00:02:26,050
As the heiress of Cheongma,

24
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:28,850
I also gave you radiant wings.

25
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,290
You are...

26
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:34,290
my...

27
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:36,220
greatest masterpiece.

28
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:38,960
You know that, right?

29
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:23,970
Being over there,

30
00:03:25,370 --> 00:03:27,110
are you happy, Kim Jung Sun?

31
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:33,280
That spot was supposed to be mine.

32
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,990
(Year 1975)

33
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,160
Hello.

34
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:47,100
My name is Joo Ae Sook, and I am seven years old.

35
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:49,500
(Hope Orphanage)

36
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:50,770
Hello.

37
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,740
My name is Joo Ae Sook, and I am seven years old.

38
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,000
You're it.

39
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,840
Wait, you didn't catch me.

40
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:00,980
- Hello. - Hey.

41
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:03,340
- I'm Joo Ae Sook, - Where are you going?

42
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,750
- and I'm seven. - You're it!

43
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:06,650
Hey, you're it.

44
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:09,620
There, I got you.

45
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,850
- You're it. - No, you're it.

46
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:15,190
Ma'am, this is Ae Sook.

47
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:17,990
She's the brightest child we have at the orphanage.

48
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:20,760
She can already read and write.

49
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:23,230
Hello.

50
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:27,070
My name is Joo Ae Sook, and I am seven years old.

51
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,610
How long have you been here?

52
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:33,240
I heard I came here when I was three.

53
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,850
She has never once resented her parents.

54
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:39,510
She's so mature and thoughtful.

55
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,880
It is an honour to meet you.

56
00:04:45,550 --> 00:04:47,220
What do you think, ma'am?

57
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:56,300
Can you get the process started?

58
00:04:57,230 --> 00:04:59,630
The child is so well-behaved and bright.

59
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,670
Ae Sook, you must greet her properly.

60
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:06,240
She's going to be your mother now.

61
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:08,880
Thank you.

62
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:11,380
Mother.

63
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:21,520
- Have you been well? - Yes.

64
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:25,190
Ae Sook, go and wait in the car.

65
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:27,030
Okay.

66
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,470
(Hope Orphanage)

67
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:34,000
Ae Sook has been looking forward to this so much.

68
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:38,210
So cool.

69
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,380
It's pretty.

70
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,850
Hey, don't. Stop that.

71
00:05:45,010 --> 00:05:46,250
Do you want this?

72
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,680
Get it away from me.

73
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,520
But this is pretty.

74
00:05:53,450 --> 00:05:57,830
Jung Sun, look at the state of you. Hurry and get inside.

75
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,960
Okay.

76
00:06:05,030 --> 00:06:06,200
Ma'am.

77
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,900
This is for you.

78
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:11,070
Your clothes are so pretty.

79
00:06:19,410 --> 00:06:23,620
Ma'am, you have to put it in water so it doesn't wilt.

80
00:06:23,990 --> 00:06:26,020
Otherwise, it'll die.

81
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:28,790
Jung Sun, let's play. Hurry up.

82
00:06:28,790 --> 00:06:30,260
Sure. Hold on.

83
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:50,980
Director, who is that child?

84
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:52,310
Oh, her?

85
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:56,020
That's Kim Jung Sun. She came here last year.

86
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,850
That's how she always is.

87
00:06:57,950 --> 00:07:01,190
She's a bit clueless, doesn't greet people properly,

88
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:02,960
and she still can't really read.

89
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:04,960
The child is...

90
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:06,890
so carefree...

91
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,660
and uncalculating.

92
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:11,030
Pardon?

93
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:14,900
Director,

94
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,540
I'm so sorry to ask,

95
00:07:18,370 --> 00:07:20,940
but could I adopt that child instead?

96
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:24,150
But, ma'am...

97
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:28,950
We already told Ae Sook she was being adopted,

98
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:31,150
and we even dressed her in new clothes.

99
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:35,790
I feel like Ae Sook will get adopted even if it isn't by me.

100
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,530
I'm begging you.

101
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,000
Please let me take the other child instead.

102
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,470
Oh, dear.

103
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,690
My gosh, you scared me.

104
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:39,850
Director Joo?

105
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:44,230
What are you doing here with the lights off?

106
00:08:45,930 --> 00:08:49,360
I came out to get some water, and the picture frame was crooked.

107
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:51,900
You startled me.

108
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:54,970
Did you need something?

109
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:58,440
I was thirsty too. I can get it.

110
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:02,440
Well, I'll go back to my room then. Good night.

111
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,850
Okay.

112
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:31,370
You know next week is the anniversary...

113
00:09:31,370 --> 00:09:32,570
of my mom's death, right?

114
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:36,780
- Has it been that long already? - Yes.

115
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,350
Hae Ra, don't make other plans.

116
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:40,980
Got it.

117
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:42,180
Ma'am.

118
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:44,250
For this year's memorial,

119
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:46,050
should I prepare those same yellow wildflowers...

120
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,120
you always bring to the columbarium?

121
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:49,620
What?

122
00:09:49,890 --> 00:09:53,190
Your late mother was so elegant and graceful,

123
00:09:53,430 --> 00:09:57,130
but she had a peculiar fondness for those tacky roadside flowers.

124
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,770
She said they held a special memory between you two.

125
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:02,570
Is that so?

126
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,540
Mom, what special memory did you have with Grandma?

127
00:10:07,610 --> 00:10:10,310
I don't know. I've forgotten it all.

128
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:13,710
Your mother had some unusual tastes, didn't she?

129
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,650
Come to think of it,

130
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:18,520
you don't seem to resemble your mother much at all.

131
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:20,920
Not in personality or in looks.

132
00:10:21,590 --> 00:10:24,990
What? What do you mean we're not alike?

133
00:10:25,530 --> 00:10:27,700
I like wildflowers too.

134
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,970
I think I'll start with a part-time job.

135
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,910
A part-time job? What about your business?

136
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,710
The more I think about it,

137
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:48,120
jumping in without any experience seems like a shortcut to failure.

138
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,790
To see if it's right for me,

139
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:53,150
I'll try working in a field I'm interested in...

140
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:54,790
for one year at a time before deciding.

141
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,630
That's a very good idea.

142
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:01,860
Instead of just thinking about it endlessly,

143
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:03,800
it's much better to get some hands-on experience.

144
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:05,330
So, have you looked for any part-time jobs?

145
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:08,400
Actually, a cafe called me in for an interview today,

146
00:11:08,470 --> 00:11:09,470
so I'll be going.

147
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:13,740
What about you, Dad?

148
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,580
Well,

149
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,410
no place will hire a man my age.

150
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:19,850
By day I'll deliver on a motorcycle,

151
00:11:19,910 --> 00:11:22,650
and by night I'll work as a designated driver.

152
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,890
That's too much, Dad. Just pick one.

153
00:11:25,950 --> 00:11:29,420
She's right. If you get sick, the medical bills will cost more.

154
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:31,260
I'll give it try for now.

155
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:35,030
Mom. Come on out and eat.

156
00:11:35,330 --> 00:11:38,270
(Maternity Handbook)

157
00:11:40,230 --> 00:11:41,240
Did you say 500,000 dollars?

158
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:42,540
Wait.

159
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,470
Did Eun Seol's birth mom really say she'd give you 500,000 dollars?

160
00:11:46,410 --> 00:11:48,240
That said, you have to give me your word.

161
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,110
Promise you'll never mistreat Eun Seol again.

162
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,550
Why would I mistreat her?

163
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:55,180
Not when there's 500,000 dollars involved.

164
00:11:59,850 --> 00:12:01,360
Why aren't you joining us for breakfast?

165
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:07,190
When did you take this?

166
00:12:08,330 --> 00:12:10,130
Son, let's find...

167
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:12,630
Eun Seol's biological mother.

168
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:16,140
I told you to pretend you never saw it.

169
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,410
How can I unseen what I've already seen?

170
00:12:19,770 --> 00:12:20,810
Don't be like that,

171
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:23,680
and tell Eun Seol to find her birth mother.

172
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:28,750
Didn't you call her a wicked woman who ran off and abandoned her baby?

173
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:30,280
So why the sudden change of heart?

174
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,590
Don't you remember?

175
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:35,290
Eun Seol's birth mother promised us half a million dollars.

176
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,090
So what?

177
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:41,430
You want to find her birth mother just to get the money?

178
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:44,700
That was 500,000 dollars a decade ago.

179
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,800
Surely we should be getting at least a million dollars now.

180
00:12:50,570 --> 00:12:51,570
Mom.

181
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,640
Eun Seol...

182
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,740
She suffered terribly...

183
00:12:55,810 --> 00:12:58,150
just to get justice for her mom after being framed for her murder.

184
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:00,680
And you want to use her to extort money...

185
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,950
from her birth mother?

186
00:13:03,150 --> 00:13:05,920
It's half a million dollars. Half a million.

187
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:09,690
I don't care if it's ten times that. From now on,

188
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,460
I'm putting Eun Seol first.

189
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,960
I made a promise to my wife.

190
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,900
It's long overdue,

191
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,470
but from now on...

192
00:13:17,770 --> 00:13:19,400
I intend to be a proper father.

193
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:20,500
So,

194
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:23,000
you need to give up on this crazy idea.

195
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:26,810
Say even a single word to Eun Seol, and I swear I won't let it go.

196
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:30,880
Oh, please.

197
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:33,210
Since when has he cared so much about Eun Seol?

198
00:13:33,350 --> 00:13:34,850
Unbelievable.

199
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:36,520
It's ridiculous.

200
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,150
Half a million dollars.

201
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,000
Mom, are you heading to the community center today?

202
00:13:51,070 --> 00:13:52,470
- Yes. - The community center bus...

203
00:13:52,470 --> 00:13:53,570
will be here soon,

204
00:13:53,570 --> 00:13:55,270
so make sure you listen to the teacher.

205
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,070
Don't worry.

206
00:13:58,070 --> 00:13:59,170
I'll be going now.

207
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:01,480
Have a good day, Mr. Seok Jin.

208
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:07,750
(Cheongma)

209
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:10,020
The upcoming Shoejoy launch will follow a two-track approach,

210
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:12,020
featuring both a premium line and a mass-market line.

211
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:14,620
How will the designs be chosen?

212
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,220
Since these will be the signature models for both lines,

213
00:14:17,290 --> 00:14:19,290
I'll decide after an internal competition...

214
00:14:19,290 --> 00:14:20,530
within the Design Team.

215
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,100
An internal competition?

216
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,430
Yes. I plan to choose based on skill alone,

217
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,500
without any bias.

218
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:28,500
Meeting the price point will be key for the mass-market line.

219
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:30,640
Can we try with synthetic leather or performance fabrics...

220
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:32,010
without any restrictions?

221
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:35,910
Even for the mass-market line, consider the target selling price...

222
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:38,810
and feel free to propose any materials you see fit.

223
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,780
What about the premium line?

224
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:43,550
Using the finest imported Italian leather...

225
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:44,790
with handcrafted details,

226
00:14:44,850 --> 00:14:46,450
can we push the price way up?

227
00:14:46,590 --> 00:14:49,160
As long as you can certainly elevate the brand's image,

228
00:14:49,190 --> 00:14:51,190
I won't impose any restrictions.

229
00:14:52,130 --> 00:14:55,230
Bring your design sketches with you to the next meeting.

230
00:14:55,230 --> 00:14:56,800
Right. Good work, everyone.

231
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,770
- Good work. - Good work.

232
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:04,870
Ms. Kang, may I go do some market research?

233
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:06,670
What market research?

234
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,010
To get inspiration for the design.

235
00:15:09,010 --> 00:15:10,210
Fine, go ahead.

236
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,550
Thank you.

237
00:15:12,610 --> 00:15:13,950
See you tomorrow.

238
00:15:17,790 --> 00:15:19,390
Can we see a movie today?

239
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,120
Aren't you going to work on your design?

240
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:23,060
Does watching a movie mean I won't work on my design?

241
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:25,060
I'll buy the tickets, okay?

242
00:15:26,090 --> 00:15:27,130
Fine.

243
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:30,430
Welcome.

244
00:15:31,770 --> 00:15:33,230
What are you doing here?

245
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,440
Mi Rae, I could ask you the same thing.

246
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,240
Do you work here?

247
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,570
Work here? Seriously? I'm the owner of this place.

248
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,680
Oh, really?

249
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,250
I had no idea.

250
00:15:45,210 --> 00:15:46,950
Well, can I get you a cup of coffee?

251
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:51,220
I didn't come here for coffee. I'm here for a job interview.

252
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:54,020
You told me to come at two o'clock.

253
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:55,590
What?

254
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,860
Were you the one on the phone yesterday?

255
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:02,030
It seems that way.

256
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:06,030
Well, this is awkward, but I'm sorry.

257
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:09,040
I have no intention of hiring you.

258
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:12,140
Why? Is it because I don't have experience?

259
00:16:13,210 --> 00:16:14,410
Didn't you say experience didn't matter...

260
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,010
as long as I was willing to work hard?

261
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:18,650
It's not about the experience.

262
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,310
Since you already live in my annex,

263
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:24,120
sharing a workplace feels a bit much, doesn't it?

264
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,560
Why would that be too much? It'd be even better.

265
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:30,820
Anyway, I have no intention of hiring you,

266
00:16:30,890 --> 00:16:32,230
so please just leave.

267
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:37,030
If you insist, I have no choice. I'll be on my way.

268
00:16:37,230 --> 00:16:38,400
Sure.

269
00:16:40,570 --> 00:16:42,400
Hello, Director.

270
00:16:44,210 --> 00:16:45,840
Teun Teun's hurt?

271
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:50,880
Okay. Yes, I'll head over now.

272
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:54,480
- Oh no. What do I do? - Wait, Teun Teun's hurt?

273
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:58,920
Yes. What should I do? I have to get to the hospital.

274
00:16:58,950 --> 00:17:01,090
Then why are you hesitating? You should hurry up.

275
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:04,120
The coffee machine repairman is supposed to come,

276
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:07,330
so I can't leave the shop unattended.

277
00:17:07,390 --> 00:17:09,560
I'll watch the shop for you, so go on.

278
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:11,930
I'll take care of it when the repairman gets here.

279
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:13,930
You will?

280
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,470
What are you waiting for? Your kid is hurt. Go on.

281
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:18,940
I hate to impose, but thank you.

282
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:31,920
(Shoe Repair)

283
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,100
Hello, sir.

284
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:50,140
Welcome. Are you here for a shoe repair?

285
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:51,840
No, nothing like that.

286
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:53,970
I was hoping to ask you a few questions.

287
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,740
First, please take this.

288
00:17:56,810 --> 00:17:58,750
You shouldn't have.

289
00:17:58,750 --> 00:18:00,710
- Have a seat. - Thanks.

290
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:05,690
So, what did you want to ask me?

291
00:18:06,150 --> 00:18:09,390
Well, I'm working on a shoe design,

292
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:11,290
and of all the people I know,

293
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:14,130
you're the one who knows the most about shoes.

294
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:16,260
You're right about that.

295
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,270
Ask me anything.

296
00:18:18,330 --> 00:18:21,000
I'll answer to the best of my ability.

297
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,200
Really?

298
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,540
Thank you so much, sir.

299
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:31,250
Stop it.

300
00:18:32,250 --> 00:18:33,480
This is hilarious.

301
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:37,420
What is wrong with you all? Just stop it.

302
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:40,520
What do you mean, "stop it," lady?

303
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,990
Getting us some cigarettes isn't that hard.

304
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:47,190
Cigarettes are bad for you, so no.

305
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:49,000
Now, move.

306
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:54,870
Just do what you're told. Who asked for your advice?

307
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:58,140
- Why are you doing this? - You're asking for it.

308
00:18:58,510 --> 00:18:59,840
What the heck?

309
00:19:00,570 --> 00:19:02,580
You shouldn't treat an adult like this.

310
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,110
Let her go.

311
00:19:12,790 --> 00:19:14,120
Darn it.

312
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:18,590
That lady's not an adult. She's a child.

313
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,690
Then what you're doing is even worse.

314
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,230
Hey, let go of me.

315
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:30,100
So what will it be?

316
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,910
Should I call the police?

317
00:19:32,110 --> 00:19:33,210
So annoying.

318
00:19:33,970 --> 00:19:35,540
Come on. Let's go, guys.

319
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:41,850
Are you all right? You must've been very scared.

320
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:45,850
I want to make a phone call.

321
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,860
Would you like me to dial for you?

322
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:54,330
I can make the call myself.

323
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,970
Take your time.

324
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:05,770
I'll stay here with you.

325
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:17,920
Hello?

326
00:20:19,190 --> 00:20:20,450
What's wrong with your voice?

327
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:25,660
What? Okay, got it. I'm on my way.

328
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:29,130
Let's go, Seok Jin.

329
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:31,270
Should we see a movie first or have dinner?

330
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:32,670
I'll have to take a rain check on the movie.

331
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:34,130
I think something's happened to my mom.

332
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,070
- I'll see you tomorrow. - Seok Jin!

333
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,710
What the heck?

334
00:20:40,210 --> 00:20:42,280
His mom is always the problem.

335
00:20:45,110 --> 00:20:47,450
Are you feeling a little better now?

336
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:51,490
Where do you live? I can walk you home.

337
00:20:52,650 --> 00:20:54,660
You'd really do that for me?

338
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:56,220
Of course.

339
00:20:57,620 --> 00:20:59,090
Thank you, Miss.

340
00:20:59,930 --> 00:21:01,900
Well, I live...

341
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:05,830
Oh, right. It's that way.

342
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,730
Okay, let's go.

343
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:16,010
This way.

344
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:20,910
This is my house.

345
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:24,280
Okay, you should go inside. I'll be on my way now.

346
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,220
Wait, you're just leaving?

347
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:29,690
You know, I was told...

348
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,730
that you should always repay a kindness.

349
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:34,190
That's okay. You should hurry inside.

350
00:21:34,290 --> 00:21:36,030
I'll leave after I see you're safely inside.

351
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:39,470
Goodbye then, nice lady.

352
00:21:39,730 --> 00:21:42,770
Thank you so much for today.

353
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,640
You're welcome.

354
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:23,940
The person you are trying to reach is unavailable.

355
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:30,780
The person you are trying to reach...

356
00:22:49,540 --> 00:22:52,710
Mom! Mom, where are you? Mom!

357
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:54,680
Hey, you're here.

358
00:22:55,310 --> 00:22:58,580
Mom, are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

359
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:02,780
A nice lady helped me, so I didn't get hurt at all.

360
00:23:04,650 --> 00:23:06,350
Wait.

361
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:09,060
Didn't you see the nice lady on your way?

362
00:23:09,590 --> 00:23:11,790
The woman who helped you came all the way here?

363
00:23:12,230 --> 00:23:15,430
Yes. She walked me right to the front door.

364
00:23:15,530 --> 00:23:17,430
She was so kind.

365
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,800
You should've gotten her phone number...

366
00:23:19,870 --> 00:23:21,070
so I could've thanked her.

367
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:23,540
Oh, I completely forgot.

368
00:23:25,910 --> 00:23:28,280
- Anyway, I'm just glad you're safe. - Right.

369
00:23:47,330 --> 00:23:48,600
Eun Seol.

370
00:23:49,500 --> 00:23:50,700
Ma'am.

371
00:23:51,770 --> 00:23:55,040
Why are you heading back up instead of going home?

372
00:23:55,570 --> 00:23:58,140
I just came from interviewing the shoe artisans,

373
00:23:58,240 --> 00:23:59,670
and I was afraid I'd forget their feedback.

374
00:23:59,770 --> 00:24:02,310
I wanted to touch up my sketches before heading home.

375
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:07,380
Did you at least have dinner?

376
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:10,020
I grabbed a quick bite on my way.

377
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:12,390
Then...

378
00:24:12,820 --> 00:24:14,690
How about joining me for a cup of tea in my office?

379
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:18,830
Ma'am, weren't you on your way home?

380
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:22,330
A few more minutes won't hurt.

381
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:23,700
Come on.

382
00:24:26,570 --> 00:24:29,400
Go ahead, try it. It's dried mugwort tea.

383
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:31,470
I'm not sure if you'll like it.

384
00:24:32,140 --> 00:24:33,670
Thank you, ma'am.

385
00:24:39,310 --> 00:24:41,280
It tastes a bit puckery and bitter, doesn't it?

386
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:43,380
Would you like some honey in it?

387
00:24:44,180 --> 00:24:46,020
No, thank you, it's fine.

388
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,750
I actually find the bitter aftertaste...

389
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:49,660
to be quite refreshing and pleasant.

390
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:53,030
- No way. You feel that way too? - Pardon me?

391
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:57,700
I like the bitterness, so I drink it without honey too.

392
00:24:58,870 --> 00:25:01,130
Hae Ra has the palate of a child...

393
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,640
and won't drink tea unless it's sweet and milky.

394
00:25:04,370 --> 00:25:07,510
It seems you and I have similar tastes.

395
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,510
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation, Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

396
00:25:12,580 --> 00:25:15,250
This is for you, Eun Seol.

397
00:25:16,380 --> 00:25:18,020
What is it?

398
00:25:18,690 --> 00:25:21,050
While getting a fountain pen for Hae Ra to sketch with,

399
00:25:21,460 --> 00:25:23,390
you crossed my mind, so I bought you one as well.

400
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:25,930
They say that for a designer,

401
00:25:25,930 --> 00:25:28,360
a pen that fits their hand just right is everything.

402
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:31,900
Why would you buy this for me?

403
00:25:32,570 --> 00:25:35,570
I heard you even refused the compensation from the company.

404
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:38,940
This is just a small gift...

405
00:25:39,270 --> 00:25:41,880
to congratulate you on clearing your name.

406
00:25:42,910 --> 00:25:44,210
So please, don't feel burdened.

407
00:25:46,110 --> 00:25:47,110
But...

408
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,050
Go on, open it.

409
00:25:55,860 --> 00:25:59,730
Ma'am, this is too generous.

410
00:26:00,890 --> 00:26:02,130
Do you like it?

411
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:04,770
Yes, but...

412
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,300
As long as you like it, that's all that matters.

413
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:14,170
You may not believe me,

414
00:26:14,940 --> 00:26:17,440
but I trusted you from the start, Eun Seol.

415
00:26:19,310 --> 00:26:21,250
I knew someone with such honest eyes...

416
00:26:22,020 --> 00:26:24,450
could never have done something so horrible.

417
00:26:26,690 --> 00:26:29,460
Thinking of how scared and lonely you must have been...

418
00:26:30,120 --> 00:26:32,560
makes my heart ache.

419
00:26:36,230 --> 00:26:39,500
Your words alone give me strength.

420
00:26:40,370 --> 00:26:41,670
Thank you, ma'am.

421
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:48,040
Use that pen to sketch...

422
00:26:48,510 --> 00:26:51,010
all of your beautiful dreams.

423
00:26:54,010 --> 00:26:55,020
I will.

424
00:26:55,820 --> 00:26:58,490
Thank you so, so much, ma'am.

425
00:26:59,750 --> 00:27:02,190
I'll always be here rooting for you.

426
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:06,160
Goodness.

427
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:20,210
Hey, what's wrong? What happened now?

428
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:23,340
Did something happen between Chief Cha and Ko Eun Seol again?

429
00:27:24,850 --> 00:27:28,080
It's not Ko Eun Seol this time. Ms. Park is the real problem.

430
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:29,550
Seok Jin's mom.

431
00:27:30,620 --> 00:27:33,350
So Yeon? Why? What is it now?

432
00:27:33,850 --> 00:27:35,890
She calls her son over for every little thing.

433
00:27:36,390 --> 00:27:38,190
We were supposed to go to the movies today,

434
00:27:38,330 --> 00:27:40,890
but he rushed off saying something happened with his mom.

435
00:27:42,060 --> 00:27:45,570
I swear, because of that woman, we can never have a proper date.

436
00:27:45,770 --> 00:27:47,900
You were aware of her condition before you began dating him.

437
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:51,610
You knew what you were getting into. Why are you acting so childish now?

438
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:53,840
I think I really need to end things with Seok Jin.

439
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:56,810
Honestly, I can't imagine living with his mother,

440
00:27:57,240 --> 00:28:00,210
and I can't stand the humiliation of always being his second priority.

441
00:28:01,350 --> 00:28:04,020
Are you prepared to stand by that?

442
00:28:06,350 --> 00:28:07,450
Stand by what?

443
00:28:07,950 --> 00:28:09,590
Why should I have to put up with this?

444
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:11,660
The second you say something like that,

445
00:28:11,990 --> 00:28:14,560
it can't be undone if it reaches the CEO's ears.

446
00:28:17,730 --> 00:28:20,030
The CEO would welcome it with open arms.

447
00:28:20,430 --> 00:28:23,470
And you think the Chairman is going to try and stop you?

448
00:28:23,870 --> 00:28:24,870
Not a chance.

449
00:28:25,470 --> 00:28:27,640
The second you call this off,

450
00:28:28,510 --> 00:28:31,650
Ms. Kim will begin searching for someone else to set you up with.

451
00:28:35,780 --> 00:28:37,580
Then what am I supposed to do?

452
00:28:38,420 --> 00:28:40,890
Just put up with all of this for the rest of my life?

453
00:28:43,690 --> 00:28:46,190
I'll figure out what to do about So Yeon.

454
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:49,530
So please, stop being so emotional.

455
00:28:50,830 --> 00:28:53,030
You can't let go of Chief Cha.

456
00:28:54,030 --> 00:28:55,740
Can you live without him?

457
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:57,370
You think I don't know you?

458
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:04,010
Director Joo, can you really take care of her for me?

459
00:29:05,650 --> 00:29:07,710
There's always a way if you look for it.

460
00:29:08,620 --> 00:29:10,620
You think I can't handle something like that?

461
00:29:13,350 --> 00:29:14,920
Then I'm counting on you, Director Joo.

462
00:29:16,590 --> 00:29:17,690
You can count on me.

463
00:29:25,770 --> 00:29:30,000
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation, Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

464
00:30:07,870 --> 00:30:11,710
(A Trap Called Desire)

465
00:30:11,780 --> 00:30:13,780
How's the internal competition going?

466
00:30:13,850 --> 00:30:15,780
Don't worry. I'm your daughter, after all.

467
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:18,650
Aren't you curious about your birth mother?

468
00:30:18,790 --> 00:30:22,060
It's 500,000 dollars. Half a million dollars.

469
00:30:22,620 --> 00:30:23,620
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

470
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,430
Knowing she was Seok Jin's mom,

471
00:30:25,490 --> 00:30:27,590
you deliberately helped her, didn't you?

472
00:30:27,790 --> 00:30:31,130
Chief Cha, do you really have to go right now?

473
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:34,270
The harder something is to get, the more it's worth.

474
00:30:34,370 --> 00:30:36,470
Shouldn't you just do what you're told?

475
00:30:36,770 --> 00:30:39,110
I want to try and track down my birth mother.

476
00:30:39,270 --> 00:30:41,710
You're very uncomfortable around me, aren't you, Eun Seol?

477
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:42,840
Did you know?

478
00:30:43,010 --> 00:30:44,680
I was one of Manager Na's victims too.
